WEBVTT

NOTE PoSE explainer, silent video. Cues repeat the on-screen text.

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.000
PoSE
Bayesian Distribution System State Estimation with Flow Matching

2
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:07.850
A medium-voltage feeder is measured at the primary substation and at a few remote points.

3
00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:10.400
What is the state everywhere else?

4
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.600
Weighted least squares reduces each substation to a mean and a variance.

5
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.600
Rooftop PV makes midday injections non-Gaussian and correlated across substations.

6
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:27.000
Deep learning estimators trained on measurement–state pairs also learn the power flow and one measurement set.

7
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.900
New meters, noise level or topology: retrain.

8
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:38.700
PoSE learns only what the operator does not know.
Known: power flow, topology, sensor locations and noise → likelihood
Unknown: the joint distribution of the injections → learned prior

9
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:49.300
A flow matching prior, trained once on historical data, transports noise to injections.

10
00:00:49.600 --> 00:01:00.300
At every step, a noise-aware Kalman-type correction pulls the estimate towards the measurements.

11
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.250
Every posterior sample is a physically consistent operating point.

12
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:08.000
One trained prior serves any measurement set, noise level and topology.

13
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:13.100
Add measurements and the posterior tightens. WLS, beside each cloud, uses Gaussian pseudo-measurements.

14
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:20.300
A typical midday test snapshot. Here PoSE's advantage over WLS equals its median advantage across the test snapshots of this setting.

15
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:28.200
Every substation is metered except bus 13. Its cloud stays wide, because the feeder-head measurement is too coarse to pin down a single substation.

16
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:36.000
6.7–7.5%
lower injection CRPS than a full-covariance Gaussian prior
IEEE 33-bus feeder with three years of measured load and rooftop PV, in all 12 settings

17
00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:43.500
0.870–0.877
coverage of the 90% intervals, against an attainable 0.882
Supervised estimators cover 37–78%

18
00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:51.000
240-bus
unbalanced three-phase Iowa feeder
lowest injection, voltage and branch-current errors of all estimators

19
00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:58.500
0.2–0.6 s
per snapshot with PoSE-fast, at the same accuracy
Without retraining, it beats Gaussian priors and retrained supervised estimators on seven reconfigured topologies

20
00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:12.500
PoSE
Bayesian Distribution System State Estimation with Flow Matching
Nan Lin, Peter Palensky, Pedro P. Vergara
Delft University of Technology
